  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "For example:\r\n\r\n\u314E + \u314F + \u3131 = <b>\uD559</b>  (hak)\r\n\u3131
    + \u315B = <b>\uAD50</b>  (gyo)\r\n\r\nPut those two blocks together and you
    get <b>\uD559\uAD50</b> \u2014 <i>school</i>.\r\n\n<size=120%><b>Good to know</b></size>\n\n<b>\u3147
    is silent at the start.</b> Every syllable needs a starting consonant, so when
    a syllable begins with a vowel sound, \u3147 fills the space and makes no sound
    of its own. That's why <b>\uC774</b> is written \u3147 + \u3163 but simply sounds
    like \"ee\"."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f1df3c7ddff326442935824dfd206057, type: 2}
